---
description: Jev paper trader project rules
alwaysApply: true
---
- This is a PAPER TRADING system. Never write code that places real orders, holds private keys, or connects funds.
- Architecture: code computes state → Jev answers narrow judgments → code policy picks action → risk engine can veto anything.
- Never put arithmetic or thresholds in Jev prompts. Thresholds live in config.yaml.
- All Jev calls go through one module (decision/jev_client.py) behind an interface, so it can be mocked.
- Pin Jev model version; log version, latency, and full answers with every call.
- If a decision arrives after the next block, it is stale: skip it.
- Every state field uses past data only. No lookahead.
- Every fill and every cancel is charged fees + gas in the simulator.
- Log everything as JSONL under logs/. Write tests for each module. Python 3.10+, type hints, small files.
